## Summary
There's no UI to remove a single text animator. Selecting an animator in the Timeline and pressing **Delete** deletes the **entire layer** instead of just the animator. In After Effects, Delete removes only the selected animator (same for masks and shape groups).

## Steps to reproduce
1. Create a text layer, Animation ▸ Animate Text ▸ Tracking.
2. In the Timeline, click the "Animator 1" group.
3. Press Delete. The whole text layer is deleted.

## Cause
- `prop.select` also selects the owning layer (`selected_layers = [lid]`).
- `edit.clear` (`crates/engine/src/commands/edit.rs`, `delete`) checks text edit, keys, mask vertices, puppet pins and effects, then falls back to deleting the selected **layers**. Selected property groups are never considered.
- `prop.removeGroup` exists and handles animators, masks, shape items and trackers, but no menu, shortcut or context menu calls it. The only UI option is Animation ▸ Remove All Text Animators.

## Suggested fix
Before the layer fallback in `edit.clear`, remove the selected instance groups (the same `is_instance` check `prop.removeGroup` uses):

```diff
--- a/crates/engine/src/commands/edit.rs
     if p.get("layers").is_none() && !super::effect::selected_effects(s).is_empty() {
         return s.execute("effect.remove", json!({}));
     }
+    // Text animators, masks, shape items selected → remove those groups (not their layer).
+    if p.get("layers").is_none() {
+        let groups = super::prop_groups::selected_instances(s);
+        if !groups.is_empty() {
+            return super::prop_groups::remove_selected(s, groups);
+        }
+    }
     let (cid, ids) = layers_p(s, p)?;
--- a/crates/engine/src/commands/prop_groups.rs
