Found while porting [LazyMapLayers](https://github.com/raisulsohan/lazymaplayers-effectcraft) (a map design and map animation panel for After Effects) to EffectCraft. Its host script runs in EffectCraft with a small compatibility layer, and all 369 kinds of expression it generates match After Effects after the workarounds: thank you for EffectCraft!

**Tested with** EffectCraft 0.8.0, Windows x64 (portable zip), headless: `effectcraft-cli script repro.jsx --empty`. The "Actual" output below is from that run.

**What happens.** File I/O is text only. Reading a PNG with `encoding = "BINARY"` decodes it as
UTF-8: its first byte 0x89 comes back as U+FFFD. In an earlier test in the app (with *Allow
Scripts to Write Files and Access Network* on), `File.copy` and writing with `"BINARY"` turned 0x89
into the bytes EF BF BD, so a copied PNG was corrupt.

**What After Effects does.** With `"BINARY"` each character is one byte (0 to 255) both ways, and
`File.copy` copies the bytes.

**Repro.** Put a PNG `sig.bin` next to a saved project and run
`effectcraft-cli script repro.jsx folder/project.ecproj` (change `dir`):

```js
var dir = "C:/path/to/folder";
var f = new File(dir + "/sig.bin");
f.encoding = "BINARY";
f.open("r");
var s = f.read();
f.close();
var codes = [];
for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) codes.push(s.charCodeAt(i).toString(16));
writeLn(codes.join(" "));
```

**Expected (After Effects).** `89 50 4e 47 d a 1a a`

**Actual (EffectCraft 0.8.0).** `fffd 50 4e 47 d a 1a a`

**How LazyMapLayers works around it.** Its companion program (Node) copies and writes binary files;
the host script only reads and writes text.

Found while bringing [LazyMapLayers for EffectCraft](https://github.com/raisulsohan/lazymaplayers-effectcraft) to LazyMapLayers 1.2 (a map design and map animation panel for After Effects, running in EffectCraft). Its 621 kinds of generated expression all match After Effects in EffectCraft: thank you!

