## Summary

The text animator's **Tracking Amount** uses different units from After Effects. In After Effects an animated Tracking Amount of 100 adds 100 px between every pair of neighbouring characters, regardless of font size. In EffectCraft it adds 1/1000 em per unit (100 = 0.1 em), the same as the static Character-panel tracking. Character spread in tracking-based reveals is several times smaller than in After Effects, and how much smaller depends on the font size.

## Environment

- effectcraft-cli 0.10.0 (`effectcraft-cli-0.10.0-macos-universal.zip`), headless
- macOS 26.3, Apple silicon
- Compared with After Effects 2026 (26.5), same font (Arial Bold) installed on the machine

## Repro

```js
var c = app.project.items.addComp("repro", 1920, 1080, 1, 5, 25);
function width(size, amount) {
  var t = c.layers.addText("ABCDE"), sp = t.property("ADBE Text Properties").property("ADBE Text Document"), d = sp.value;
  d.resetCharStyle(); d.font = "Arial-BoldMT"; d.fontSize = size; d.justification = ParagraphJustification.LEFT_JUSTIFY; sp.setValue(d);
  t.property("ADBE Text Properties").property("ADBE Text Animators").addProperty("ADBE Text Animator");
  var props = t.property("ADBE Text Properties").property("ADBE Text Animators").property(1).property("ADBE Text Animator Properties");
  props.addProperty("ADBE Text Tracking Amount");
  var p = props.property("ADBE Text Tracking Amount") || props.property("tracking");   // EffectCraft name, see #1063
  p.setValue(amount);
  var w = t.sourceRectAtTime(0, false).width; t.remove(); return Math.round(w);
}
"50px " + width(50, 0) + " -> " + width(50, 100) + ", 200px " + width(200, 0) + " -> " + width(200, 100);
```

| Width of "ABCDE" (4 gaps) | 50 px, amount 0 → 100 | 200 px, amount 0 → 100 |
|---|---|---|
| After Effects 2026 | 175 → **575** (+400, 100 px per gap) | 701 → **1101** (+400, 100 px per gap) |
| EffectCraft 0.10.0 | 175 → 195 (+20, 0.1 em per gap) | 701 → 781 (+80, 0.1 em per gap) |

